.SS Filters
.PP
In the mail directory a file named \f[V]Filters.txt\f[R] is filled in
with filtering rules referencing the contents of the \f[B]From:\f[R] or
\f[B]To:\f[R] fields.
.PP
The format of the filters configurarion is pretty easy and self
explanatory, just have a look at this file and when something changes
update the filter engine using \f[V]jaro update\f[R].
.PP
Then use \f[V]jaro filter any-maildir/\f[R] and the mails contained in
\f[V]any-maildir\f[R] will be moved according to the updated filter
rules.
.PP
Beware that filtering is a lengthy operation, especially on big
maildirs.
.SS Merge maildirs
.PP
Mblaze can safely move all e-mails stored in one maildir to another.
.PP
\f[V]mlist latest-mails | mrefile global-archive\f[R]
.PP
The above command will move all emails stored inside the maildir folder
\f[V]latest-mails\f[R] to the other maildir folder
\f[V]global-archive\f[R].
.SS Backup mails
.PP
Backup strategies can be easily managed: just move all emails older than
a certain period from one maildir to another.
.PP
Using jaromail search function with date we obtain a list of matches and
process them using mblaze\[cq]s \f[V]mrefile\f[R] command:
.PP
For instance to move all archived mails older than 3 years into a
separate folder:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
jaro search date:3y.. | mrefile /media/backup/old-mails
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
This will move into the maildir \f[V]/media/backup/old.mails\f[R] all
the emails older than 3 years that are found in any folder.
.PP
One can also use \f[B]jaro link\f[R] to create symlinks into a new
maildir: to review results without increasing filesystem occupation,
then open the destination maildir normally using
\f[V]neomutt -r -f destination/\f[R]
.SS Security
.PP
We love to keep our own email private, this is how jaromail does it.
.SS Password storage
.PP
Our MUA (Mutt), MTA (Fetchmail) and SMTP (msmtp) require the user to
input account passwords every time they run, jeopardizing their secrecy.
.PP
Jaromail saves and provides passwords to these components without saving
them on the filesystem in clear: they are stored securely through
password-store (https://www.passwordstore.org/) (also known as
\f[V]pass\f[R], the standard UNIX password manager).
We save All passwords in the \f[V]$HOME/.password-store\f[R] GPG
encrypted database under the \f[V]email/\f[R] path followed by the main
account email.
.SS Secure storage
.PP
Jaromail is fully compatible with \f[B]Tomb, the Crypto Undertaker\f[R]
[2] another Dyne.org softwareto manage encrypted volumes.
.PP
Using a light combination of scripts between Jaromail and Tomb is
possible to achieve a strong level of personal security, definitely
above the average.
.PP
In particular, Jaro Mail does not needs system-wide installation, but
can be installed and used in a way that makes it totally self-contained
and transportable across systems inside a Tomb.
.SS Anonymous emails
.PP
To send an anonymous email just change the \f[I]From:\f[R] header field
to \f[V]anon\[at]mixmaster\f[R].
Our application will recognize that as a request to send the email
across the MixMaster anonymous network.
.PP
To change \f[I]From:\f[R] in Mutt: after composition, when headers and
attachments are shown, press \f[B]ESC\f[R] and then \f[B]f\f[R], then
type the special sender address \f[V]anon\[at]mixmaster\f[R] and press
\f[B][Enter]\f[R].
.SS Shell environment
.SS Zsh commandline completion
.PP
For Zsh users out there there is a completion recipe that can facilitate
the use of Jaro Mail by adding tab completion on the console terminal:
commands and accounts will be listed and completed automatically just
like with other commands.
.PP
To activate the completion move the file
\f[B]src/completion/_jaromail\f[R] into the path where zsh loads vendor
completions, typically that is
\f[B]/usr/share/zsh/vendor-completions\f[R].
.SS Quickly send a file via email on Apple/OSX
.PP
To right-click on a file and send it via email attach using Jaro Mail
you must create a \[dq]Service\[dq] using the application
\[dq]Automator\[dq].
It is fairly simple:
.IP "1." 3
Start Automator
.IP "2." 3
Choose the Service template
.IP "3." 3
In the dropdown boxes that appear choose \[dq]files or folders\[dq] and
\[dq]Finder\[dq]
.IP "4." 3
Look for \[dq]Run Applescript\[dq] in the Library tree
.IP "5." 3
Drag \[dq]Run Applescript\[dq] in the workflow area and paste this
script into it:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
on run {input, parameters}
    tell application \[dq]Terminal\[dq]
        activate
        tell window 1
            do script \[dq]/Applications/JaroMail.app/Contents/Resources/jaro/bin/jaro \[dq] & POSIX path of input
        end tell
    end tell
end run
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Now Save the new service (you can name it \[dq]Send file via Jaro
Mail\[dq]) and when you will right click on a file, in the submenu
\[dq]Services\[dq] you will find the option you just scripted, which
will open a Terminal asking you the email address, while the file will
be already configured as attach.
